rekey:
Script: P/sfix/tools/rekey.js (functions rekeyLang, mapSection, rekeyVerdicts).

The OLD identity code is legacy/v32: a byte copy of base32/tools' cut, common, ledger, blocks, facts, classify, rules, normalizers and gen. Its only change is that ledger.js and blocks.js record each occurrence (`occ`); `--code <dir>` names another code. Both codes cut the same output. Every old class occurrence (variation + unit texts) is found again as an identical new occurrence, or, where the new splitter cut a unit, as the new occurrences of that variation whose texts lie inside it.

Per new class:
- renamed: the record moves as is;
- merged: carried only if all old outcomes agree (a `shared:` match counts as one outcome), n set to the new count; otherwise CONFLICT, listed for a person;
- split: each part inherits, n set, listed;
- an occurrence no old class held: UNSOURCED, nothing carried.

What it maps:
- hand/<lang>.json class entries;
- hand `absent` (through the old absent list's example under the new identity);
- pinned/<lang>.json;
- classes/<lang>.json;
- counts/<lang>.json: compared, unchanged for all nine;
- purity-allow: keyed by text, untouched.

Records whose ids no class of the old code makes were stale before the re-key and are kept as they are: 18 hand, 56 pinned across the nine. Records already keyed by this code are detected and left alone, which makes a second run a no-op (control rekey-idempotent).

